# Cucut Core Standards

Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) first.

## Git flow

- **Branch first** — before any feature/fix code, `git checkout -b feature/...` or `fix/...` from `main`
- Never commit directly to `main`
- One logical change per PR
- Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`)

## Before every push

```bash
bash scripts/pre-push-check.sh
```

Enable hooks:

```bash
git config core.hooksPath .githooks
pre-commit install
pre-commit install --hook-type commit-msg
```

## Documentation

Update in the same PR as code:

- `CHANGELOG.md` → `[Unreleased]` for behaviour changes
- `README.md` / `CONTRIBUTING.md` when setup or workflow changes
- `AGENTS.md` when agent workflow changes

## Semantic versioning

- Source of truth: `pyproject.toml` `version` + `src/cucut/__init__.py` `__version__`
- Before push to `main` with app code: `bash scripts/bump-version.sh` + finalize CHANGELOG
- Service paths (`.cursor/`, `.agents/`, `scripts/`, docs-only) skip version bump — see `scripts/service-paths.list`

## Modular code

| Module | Responsibility only |
|--------|---------------------|
| `scan.py` | freezedetect batch scan → CSV rows |
| `csvio.py` | review CSV read/write |
| `segments.py` | interval math (merge, invert) |
| `ffmpeg.py` | ffprobe, freezedetect, concat trim |
| `trim.py` | lossless trim orchestration |
| `export.py` | LosslessCut CSV export |
| `gui.py` | launch external GUIs |
| `cli.py` | argparse commands only |

Do not mix CLI parsing with ffmpeg calls or CSV logic.

## DevOps

- Local validation mirrors CI (`pre-commit`, `pytest`, `ruff`)
- Never commit `.venv/`, `*.trimmed.mp4`, secrets

## Token efficiency

Use `caveman` / `cavecrew` skills when user asks for terse responses or long sessions.
